From 1e05defcb48bd063e3b2b40e2e81d43f6546347e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 13:14:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Welsh register of interests: pull all dated snapshots, not
 just newest PDF

fetch_register_of_interests previously grabbed only the single newest
register PDF linked directly on the main interests page. That page only
links direct PDFs for the older terms (1st-4th Assembly, 5th Senedd); the
most recently *completed* term (6th Senedd, 2021-2026) instead links to a
separate archive page, which the old code never followed. So "newest PDF"
resolved to the 5th Senedd's 2021 archive, matched against zero of the
current 96 members -> 0 records, exactly as the code's own prior comment
predicted, without noticing a better source existed one link away.

Confirmed live 2026-09-05 that the unfollowed 6th Senedd archive page lists
14 dated snapshots of the compiled register, roughly every 4 months from
April 2022 to 8 April 2026 (days before the 2026 election) -- a real
historical time series of declared interests, not just a single point in
time.

Added _find_register_snapshots(), which walks every register/interest link
on the main page: a direct .pdf link is one snapshot (date unknown from the
link itself, as before); a same-site page link is an archive index, which
gets fetched once to pull out every dated "... as on <date> (PDF ...)"
snapshot found there. This generically picks up any future term published
the same way, with no per-term special-casing.

fetch_register_of_interests now parses every snapshot found (all older
single-PDF terms plus all 14 dated 6th-Senedd snapshots) instead of
guessing at one "best" PDF.

_parse_interests_pdf gained snapshot_date/term parameters: an entry with no
inline date (typical for an ongoing declaration like "I am a member of
Unite...") now falls back to its own snapshot's "as on <date>" cover date
instead of being left blank -- a real, meaningful date (when the member had
this interest on record), rather than a gap. An entry-specific inline date
still takes precedence when present. Records are tagged with term and
register_snapshot_date metadata plus a date_is_snapshot_fallback flag so
the two date sources stay distinguishable downstream.

Verified with two mocked tests (this container can't reach senedd.wales):
one confirming _find_register_snapshots correctly follows the archive page
and parses "as on <date>" into ISO dates alongside the older direct-PDF
entries; one confirming _parse_interests_pdf's date-fallback/precedence
logic and metadata tagging against a synthetic PDF text extraction.

Also updated test_scrape.py's Welsh register-of-interests note, which
previously described a stale, no-longer-accurate "~200 undated entries"
symptom from a different run state than what the code now produces.

